            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0597" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg587"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/904: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stanton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-28T16:00:00+08:00">November 28,
                            1941—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 3—2:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1791. First contingent of American Marines sailed yesterday afternoon on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">President Madison</hi>. Colonel Howard with remaining
                    contingents sailed this afternoon on <hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>.
                    Stirring scenes of farewell took place at the customs jetty upon the departure
                    of the Fourth Marines. Diplomatic, consular, military and naval representatives
                    of various foreign governments were present to bid Colonel Howard and his staff
                    farewell. There was also a large turnout of members of foreign and Chinese
                    communities.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, repeated to Chungking and Peiping. Code text by air mail
                    to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
